# card pure-exit-miscompile (issue #3098): exit() never returns, so a try or an if with an exit branch takes the value
# of its other branch, inside a function as at the top level
# (`warp test tests/control` )

# a_try_whose_catch_exits_keeps_the_tried_value
is! "f() := try 42 catch e { exit(1) }
f()" 42
is! "x = try 42 catch e { exit(1) }
x" 42

# an_if_whose_else_exits_keeps_the_then_value
is! "f(x) := if x > 0 { x } else { exit(1) }
f(42)" 42
is! "g() := exit(1)
f(x) := if x > 0 { x } else { g() }
f(42)" 42
